{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.HadronUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.HadronUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.HadronDisplay"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hadron.unique_up_to_isotopy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hadron.unique_up_to_isotopy","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-unique.lean#L55-L71","doc":"**Uniqueness of hadrons up to isotopy (proved).**\n\nIsotopy-equivalent hadrons are equal: the base-point coordinates\nand constituent list are shared, and the length constraint is\npropositional.  This replaces a false `Subsingleton Hadron` axiom\n(from which `False` was derivable) with a genuinely proved\nstatement at the equivalence-relation level. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hadron-unique","label":"prop:hadron-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hadron.isotopyEquiv_equivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hadron.isotopyEquiv_equivalence","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-unique.lean#L47-L53","doc":"Isotopy equivalence is an equivalence relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hadron.IsotopyEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hadron.IsotopyEquiv","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-unique.lean#L38-L45","doc":"**Isotopy equivalence of hadrons.**  Two hadrons are isotopy-\nequivalent when they share the base-point coordinates on `S²` and\ntheir constituent braid words agree.  Pending a Markov-move\nrelation on `KnotTheory.BraidWord`, constituent agreement is list\nequality — the discrete core of braid isotopy. ","signatureChunk":0}]}